Why This Is Asked

Tests for frontend caching and offline behavior are common; this probes practical test design with mocks, cache TTL, offline path, and retry/backoff without backend complexity.

## Key Concepts

- Unit and integration tests for fetch + cache logic
- Mocking remote config and network conditions
- Cache invalidation TTL and rehydration after backoff
- Correct handling of offline mode and per-user overrides

## Code Example

```javascript
// sample function to fetch flags with cache
export async function getFlags(userId) {
  const cached = localStorage.getItem('flags');
  const cacheTs = Number(localStorage.getItem('flags_ts')||0);
  if (cached && Date.now() - cacheTs < 5 * 60 * 1000) {
    return JSON.parse(cached);
  }
  const resp = await fetch('/config/flags');
  const flags = await resp.json();
  localStorage.setItem('flags', JSON.stringify(flags));
  localStorage.setItem('flags_ts', String(Date.now()));
  return flags;
}
```

